To replace whitespaces with an underscore and vice versa in a given string, you can use the `replace()` method or regular expressions (regex). Below is an example using both methods:

```javascript
// Using replace() method
function replaceWhitespace(inputString) {
    return inputString.replace(/\s/g, '_').replace(/_/g, ' ');
}

// Using regex
function replaceWhitespaceWithRegex(inputString) {
    return inputString.replace(/(\s|_)/g, (match) => {
        if (match === ' ') {
            return '_';
        } else {
            return ' ';
        }
    });
}

// Example usage
